   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">By strengthening Health Emergency Operations Centre (HEOC) systems, AIHSP contributed to enhancing Indonesia&#x2019;s ability to anticipate, prevent, detect, and control communicable disease threats. HEOCs play a central role in coordinating disease surveillance, mobilising rapid response teams, and delivering timely public health messaging during health emergencies.
&#x200d;
Between July and October 2024, AIHSP worked closely with provincial health offices in South Sulawesi, Bali, Central Java, and Nusa Tenggara Timur (NTT), providing technical assistance to finalise and align provincial HEOC guidelines with national health emergency standards following simulation exercises and after-action reviews, which tested the capacity of the HEOCs to respond to health threats such as rabies and anthrax outbreaks.
&#x200d;
As a result, all four provinces officially adopted the HEOC guidelines as a multisectoral emergency response mechanism. This helps improve coordination among provincial stakeholders, clearer roles and responsibilities during public health crises, and stronger linkages between human and animal health sectors.</narrative>
    </description>
