    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since October 2022, Indonesia has reported seven cases of Polio outbreak with latest cases reported in Papua. UNICEF supported by Australia conducted advocacy meetings for high level officials along with training on vaccine management and the immunisation record mobile application Aplikasi Sehat Indonesiaku (ASIK) for immunisation and logistic managers in the impacted provinces. A total of 312 health workers were trained on vaccine management and 2,984 health care providers trained on ASIK. These efforts resulted in improved capacity for vaccine management, improved reporting on the ASIK application for better real time coverage monitoring, and stronger community engagement through active participation of local leaders. This supported national efforts which resulted in a total of 15 million children having received vaccination during the Polio outbreak response in five provinces, each reaching above 90% coverage.</narrative>
    </description>
